# Solar Wind behind Caddy (helios.solarWind.exposure = "proxy").
# Runs on a machine with a public IP (e.g. a VPS) that is on the same tailnet
# as the router. Caddy gets the TLS certificate; ntfy's streaming connections
# work through reverse_proxy as-is.
#
# Replace:
#   alerts.example.com   → the public name phones subscribe to (= helios.solarWind.publicUrl)
#   ROUTER_TAILSCALE_IP  → the router's 100.x address (`tailscale ip -4` on the router)
#   2586                 → helios.solarWind.port if you changed it
# Your tailnet policy must let this proxy reach the router on that port.

alerts.example.com {
	reverse_proxy http://ROUTER_TAILSCALE_IP:2586
}
